  "summary": "Connect external GoHighLevel sub-accounts to your workspace via OAuth.",
  "answer": "## Overview\n\nOAuth enables you to connect external GoHighLevel sub-accounts (those not natively under your GHL workspace) to your Assistable workspace. This is useful for agencies that manage clients across multiple GHL workspaces.\n\n## Setup\n\n<Steps>\n  <Step title=\"Navigate to OAuth Settings\">\n    In your Assistable workspace, go to the OAuth configuration section.\n  </Step>\n\n  <Step title=\"Generate OAuth Link\">\n    Create an OAuth authorization link for the external sub-account.\n  </Step>\n\n  <Step title=\"Authorize in GHL\">\n    Have the sub-account owner click the link and authorize the connection in GoHighLevel.\n  </Step>\n\n  <Step title=\"Verify Connection\">\n    Confirm the sub-account appears in your Assistable workspace dashboard.\n  </Step>\n</Steps>\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nSee [OAuth Configuration](/troubleshooting/oauth-configuration) for common issues and solutions.",
